======================================================================
(A') M2 STRUCTURAL: prove arc-reversal under tau->-tau (reflection).
    snrm((i-j)*(-tau)) = -snrm((i-j)*tau) (generically). So reflecting
    the lonely time reverses ALL arcs => complement tournament.
    Since g(S,tau)=g(S,1-tau) (||.|| symmetric), the lonely set is
    reflection-symmetric: if tau optimal then 1-tau is ALSO optimal.
    Check: at BOTH optimal taus we get a class and its complement; the
    REALIZED SET is thus closed under complement. Verify empirically.
======================================================================
  base n=5: realized set closed under complement (incl 1-tau)? True; #classes=4

